    "b-10-editing-model-text-commits-run-on-ever-17": {
      "id": "b-10-editing-model-text-commits-run-on-ever-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Text commits run on every keystroke. Structured inline nodes survive the round\ntrip because the editable text form re-parses "
        },
        {
          "insert": "{{name}}",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "{{kind:name}}",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "\ntokens back into variable and reference nodes."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-editing-model-steps-not-snapshots-18": {
      "id": "b-10-editing-model-steps-not-snapshots-18",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Steps, Not Snapshots"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-editing-model-block-edits-produce-step-19": {
      "id": "b-10-editing-model-block-edits-produce-step-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Block edits produce steps, insert, remove, move, update, and hand them to\nthe host alongside the resulting document:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-editing-model-ts-20": {
      "id": "b-10-editing-model-ts-20",
      "type": "code",
      "props": {
        "language": "ts"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "type PromptFlowChangeHandler = (\n  prompt: PromptDocument,\n  selectedNodeId?: string,\n  steps?: PromptStep[],\n) => void;"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-editing-model-a-change-without-steps-21": {
      "id": "b-10-editing-model-a-change-without-steps-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A change without "
        },
        {
          "insert": "steps",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is a document-metadata edit (title or description),\nwhich is not node-scoped and therefore not representable as a step. The host\ncommits steps to the transaction log and metadata to an overlay; both share\none undo/redo stack (see\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Application Shell",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/60-editor/60-application-shell"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ")."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-editing-model-a-structural-gesture-tha-22": {
      "id": "b-10-editing-model-a-structural-gesture-tha-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A structural gesture that takes two or three steps is handed over as one array\nand committed as one transaction, so one undo takes back the whole move."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-editing-model-selectednodeid-is-the-23": {
      "id": "b-10-editing-model-selectednodeid-is-the-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "selectedNodeId",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is the commit's selection echo. While an inline edit session\nis live the surface forwards it as "
        },
        {
          "insert": "undefined",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", hosts write the echo back\ninto selection state, and a keystroke must not re-select the block being typed\nin (the caret plus the edit wash is the whole treatment). Commits made outside\na live session, block menu inserts, item menu operations, drops, keep their\necho and still select deliberately."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-editing-model-caret-continuity-24": {
      "id": "b-10-editing-model-caret-continuity-24",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Caret Continuity"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-editing-model-the-surface-stores-one-e-25": {
      "id": "b-10-editing-model-the-surface-stores-one-e-25",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The surface stores one edit target: a node id, an optional item index, and a\ncaret. A caret is a numeric offset, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "\"end\"",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", or a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "[start, end]",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " pair; a\nnumber is clamped to the value's length, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "\"end\"",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " resolves to the end, and a\npair seats a selection so the next keystroke types over it."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-editing-model-structural-gestures-land-26": {
      "id": "b-10-editing-model-structural-gestures-land-26",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Structural gestures land the caret in the block they moved, at the same offset\nwhere possible, so a level change is never a reason to stop typing. Every\ncaret move re-seats the editor deliberately, a split, merge, arrow step,\nclick, or conversion each places the caret exactly once, and a stale blur\nfrom the editor being replaced can never cancel the new edit."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-editing-model-exactly-one-row-of-a-nod-27": {
      "id": "b-10-editing-model-exactly-one-row-of-a-nod-27",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Exactly one row of a node may host the editor at a time. A code block draws\ntwo fences, a section draws two tags, and a list draws a row per item; the\nsurface resolves which row owns the caret from the row's role, item index, and\ncontent line index. Two editors sharing a target would fight for focus."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-editing-model-click-to-caret-28": {
      "id": "b-10-editing-model-click-to-caret-28",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Click To Caret"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-editing-model-one-resolution-maps-a-cl-29": {
      "id": "b-10-editing-model-one-resolution-maps-a-cl-29",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "One resolution maps a click point to a caret for every editable row. The click\nresolves to a text offset in the row, then display offset maps to editable\noffset by subtracting the row's display prefix, a plain row's leading indent,\nor nothing for list-item content whose marker is drawn as separate trim. For\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "raw",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "codeBlock",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows the clicked content line index is folded back into\nan offset within the single multi-line value. A point that resolves to no text\nposition falls back to caret-at-end, never caret-at-zero."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-editing-model-headless-editor-model-30": {
      "id": "b-10-editing-model-headless-editor-model-30",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Headless Editor Model"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-editing-model-createprompteditormodel-31": {
      "id": "b-10-editing-model-createprompteditormodel-31",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "createPromptEditorModel(prompt, options)",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is the headless entry for viewers\nand hosts: it ensures stable block ids (unless asked not to), flattens the\ndocument into a tree of entries carrying path, depth, sibling, label, and\nsummary metadata, preserves a valid requested selection (falling back to the\nfirst entry), renders the document with optional runtime variables, and\nvalidates it against optionally declared variable names. The result, prompt,\nselection, tree, rendered string, validation, is plain serializable data with\nno React or DOM dependency."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    }
  }
}
